{"id":"fc1afbe4-3c6d-4a17-89f4-255244eb5813","object":"chat.completion","created":1785035388,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    root_id = None\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        pid = n.get('parent')\\n        if pid is None:\\n            root_id = n['id']\\n        else:\\n            children[pid].append(n['id'])\\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\\n    required_node_ids = {n['id'] for n in nodes if n['symbol'] in required_symbols}\\n    # verify all required symbols present initially\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if not any(n['symbol'] == sym for n in nodes):\\n            raise ValueError(f'Required symbol {sym} not present')\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    removed = []\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if not n.get('removable', False):\\n            continue\\n        if nid == root_id or nid in required_node_ids:\\n            continue\\n        # check retained children\\n        if any(cid in retained for cid in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n        # feasibility: symbol counts after removal\\n        symbol_counts = {}\\n        for sym in required_symbols:\\n            symbol_counts[sym] = 0\\n        for rid in retained:\\n            sym = node_map[rid]['symbol']\\n            if sym in required_symbols:\\n                symbol_counts[sym] += 1\\n        # subtract one if this node's symbol is required\\n        nsym = n['symbol']\\n        if nsym in required_symbols:\\n            symbol_counts[nsym] -= 1\\n        if any(count <= 0 for count in symbol_counts.values()):\\n            continue\\n        # remove\\n        removed.append(nid)\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_sorted\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that processes the given payload. The task is \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\". The description mentions Perses syntax-guided reduction on a miniature grammar. The input has nodes with parent, symbol, depth, removable flag, utility. There is also required_symbols list.\n\nWe need to decide which nodes to remove and which to retain. The goal: reduce the tree by removing nodes that are removable and not required, while preserving required symbols. The algorithm: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo we need to simulate reduction: Start with all nodes. Then iterate over nodes in order of decreasing depth (deepest first), and at equal depth, by something? The instruction says \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" and \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" So we sort nodes by depth descending, then by ID ascending (or any stable order). Then for each node, check if it is removable and not required symbol. Also check if removing it still leaves all required symbols present in the remaining tree. Additionally, we cannot remove a node that has children that are retained (i.e., if any descendant is still present, we cannot remove it? Actually \"Never remove ... a node with retained children.\" If a node has children that are retained, we cannot remove it because that would remove those children? But the children might be removed first. Since we process deeper nodes first, children will be considered before parents. So if a child is removable and we decide to remove it, then later when considering the parent, the child is already removed. But if a child is not removable, then the parent has a retained child, so parent cannot be removed. That makes sense.\n\nThus algorithm:\n- Build a set of all node IDs.\n- Build mapping from id to node dict.\n- Build children lists: for each node, add its id to parent's children list.\n- Identify root (parent null).\n- Determine required_symbols set.\n- Determine which symbols are required: nodes whose symbol is in required_symbols. Those nodes cannot be removed. Also root cannot be removed.\n- Process nodes in order: sorted by depth descending, then by id (string) ascending.\n- For each node in that order:\n    - If node is not removable, skip.\n    - If node is required (symbol in required_symbols) or is root, skip.\n    - Check if node has any children that are still retained (i.e., any child id present in current retained set). If yes, skip.\n    - Tentatively consider removal: would the remaining nodes still cover all required_symbols? That is, after removing this node, is every required symbol still present in at least one node? Note: we need to check across all nodes that are still retained (including those not yet processed). But since we are processing in order, the current set of retained nodes includes all nodes not yet removed or decided. So we can check: for each required symbol, there exists at least one node in the current retained set (including the node we are about to remove) that has that symbol and is not being removed? Actually we are checking before removal. So if we remove this node, we need to ensure that for each required symbol, there is at least one other node with that symbol that will remain. So we can count occurrences of each required symbol among retained nodes, and ensure that after removal, each required symbol count >=1. If node is the only node for a required symbol, cannot remove.\n    - If both conditions satisfied, remove the node: add to removed_node_ids list, remove from retained set.\n- After processing all nodes, the remaining nodes are retained_node_ids.\n- Sort retained_node_ids ascending (by id string) and removed_node_ids in order of removal (the order we processed and removed them). The output requires \"removed_node_ids\" and \"retained_node_ids\" both arrays of strings. \"removed_node_ids\" should be the actual removal order? The instruction says \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So removed_node_ids should be in the order nodes were removed. Retained_node_ids should be sorted.\n\nWe need to raise ValueError for infeasible cases? Possibly if required symbols not present initially, but input seems valid. We'll just assume valid, but can add check: after initial, ensure all required symbols exist; if not, raise ValueError.\n\nNow implement solve(case) function in Python.\n\nNote: The input case object is the payload (inner object). It has \"nodes\" list and \"required_symbols\" list, and maybe \"_case_nonce\" but ignore.\n\nImplementation steps:\n- Parse nodes into dicts.\n- Build retained set = set of node ids.\n- Build children map: dict id -> list of child ids.\n- Find root id: node with parent None.\n- Build required_nodes set: ids of nodes whose symbol is in required_symbols.\n- Build required_symbols_set.\n- Precompute symbol counts among all nodes. But we can compute on the fly.\n- Define order: sorted nodes, key = (-depth, id)\n- removed = []\n- For each node in order:\n    - if node['removable'] is False, continue.\n    - if node['id'] in required_nodes or node['id'] == root_id, continue.\n    - if any child_id in retained for child in children of node, continue.\n    - Check removal feasibility: for each required symbol, count occurrences in retained set (including current node). If removing this node would cause any symbol count to become 0, skip. Otherwise, remove:\n        - removed.append(node['id'])\n        - retained.remove(node['id'])\n- After loop, retained sorted = sorted(retained)\n- Return {\"removed_node_ids\": removed, \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted}\n\nEdge cases: depth may be present but we use it. Ensure we treat ids as strings.\n\nNow output JSON with \"implementation\" key containing the Python source as a string, properly escaped.\n\nWe'll write the function as def solve(case): ... and then return the code as string.\n\nMake sure to escape quotes, newlines, backslashes.\n\nWe'll produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2172,"completion_tokens":1840,"total_tokens":4012,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1325},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":124},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}